WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.387 --> 00:00:14.987
is dangerous!"

2
00:00:15.207 --> 00:00:15.807
Gliss cried.

3
00:00:15.827 --> 00:00:18.788
"There must be another way into Wormwood."

4
00:00:19.648 --> 00:00:21.529
"No, Zann is right," Perda said.

5
00:00:21.549 --> 00:00:23.529
"We can't waste time.

6
00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:26.030
Morb is already taking over Magica!"

7
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.331
"How will we reach a wormhole?"

8
00:00:28.531 --> 00:00:29.171
Darb asked.

9
00:00:29.191 --> 00:00:33.352
"There's one in the palace, but there's no way we can sneak in there."

10
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.781
"There's one in Edgewood," Perda said.

11
00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.883
"Wyssa brought us there once."

12
00:00:38.944 --> 00:00:40.285
"Perfect," Zann said.

13
00:00:40.305 --> 00:00:41.626
"Let's zap there now."

14
00:00:45.268 --> 00:00:48.330
A moment later they stood in front of the Edgewood wormhole.

15
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:51.553
"Are you sure this is a good idea?"

16
00:00:51.993 --> 00:00:52.593
Gliss asked.

17
00:00:53.254 --> 00:00:55.295
"We don't have the guidelink anymore.

18
00:00:55.796 --> 00:00:58.297
How are we going to navigate through the vortex?"

19
00:00:59.198 --> 00:00:59.919
Perda frowned.

20
00:00:59.939 --> 00:01:01.560
"Good question.

21
00:01:02.376 --> 00:01:06.139
It could take a long time to find our way to the Wormwood wormhole."

22
00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.222
"If we can find it at all," Darb said.

23
00:01:10.043 --> 00:01:10.823
Zann shrugged.

24
00:01:10.843 --> 00:01:12.805
"Do you have a better plan?

25
00:01:13.125 --> 00:01:14.907
We're wasting time arguing about this."

26
00:01:14.927 --> 00:01:19.891
"We'll waste even more time if we get lost in the vortex," Gliss said.

27
00:01:19.911 --> 00:01:22.673
"I think we should—Wyssa!"

28
00:01:23.554 --> 00:01:26.276
The old woman had just zapped into sight nearby.

29
00:01:26.296 --> 00:01:28.298
"There you are!"

30
00:01:28.638 --> 00:01:29.459
Wyssa exclaimed.

31
00:01:30.199 --> 00:01:32.804
Surprisingly, she seemed glad to see everyone.

32
00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.785
"What are you doing here?"

33
00:01:35.205 --> 00:01:35.765
Zann asked.

34
00:01:35.785 --> 00:01:37.846
"Are you trying to escape through the wormhole?"

35
00:01:38.966 --> 00:01:42.127
"No, I was looking for you, actually," Wyssa said.

36
00:01:42.147 --> 00:01:47.289
"I have something important to tell all of you—especially you."

37
00:01:48.169 --> 00:01:49.789
She jabbed a finger toward Zann.

38
00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.350
"Okay, what is it?"

39
00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:52.110
he asked.

40
00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.531
Wyssa opened her mouth to reply.

41
00:01:55.231 --> 00:01:57.632
But just then Gliss let out a scream.

42
00:02:00.556 --> 00:02:01.216
"Trolls!" she cried.

43
00:02:02.057 --> 00:02:03.097
Zann spun around.

44
00:02:03.958 --> 00:02:05.959
Half a dozen trolls were charging toward them.

45
00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:08.400
"Let's get out of here!"

46
00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:09.521
Wyssa shouted.

47
00:02:10.281 --> 00:02:13.223
She grabbed Zann with one hand and Darb with the other.

48
00:02:13.963 --> 00:02:18.726
Zann had just enough time to grab Zing's tail before the whole group dived into the wormhole.

49
00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.407
They weren't in the vortex for long.

50
00:02:22.127 --> 00:02:26.049
Before Zann could catch his breath, Wyssa tugged them toward another wormhole.

51
00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.991
Seconds later they emerged in Wormwood.

52
00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:31.640
"Whew!" Gliss exclaimed.

53
00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:33.181
"That was quick."

54
00:02:34.221 --> 00:02:35.162
Zann looked around.

55
00:02:35.182 --> 00:02:37.183
"Uh-oh," he said.

56
00:02:37.203 --> 00:02:39.484
"More trolls are coming!"

57
00:02:40.364 --> 00:02:43.425
Several trolls had been lounging in the shade of the Wormwood tree.

58
00:02:44.286 --> 00:02:46.527
Now they hurried toward Zann and the others.

59
00:02:47.447 --> 00:02:50.108
Zing flew up and whistled his distinctive song.

60
00:02:50.928 --> 00:02:54.350
The trolls slowed down and craned their necks toward the little dragon.

61
00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.651
"Hurry!" Perda whispered.

62
00:02:56.671 --> 00:02:59.232
"Let's hide while Zing distracts them."

63
00:03:00.276 --> 00:03:02.417
She led the way into a large hut nearby.

64
00:03:03.418 --> 00:03:06.179
A moment later the trolls seemed to lose interest in Zing.

65
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.702
They blinked, looked around, and then wandered off and disappeared into a different hut.

66
00:03:11.722 --> 00:03:17.125
"They're so stupid that they forgot what they were doing," Zann whispered.

67
00:03:17.145 --> 00:03:18.866
"Never mind that."

68
00:03:19.507 --> 00:03:20.807
Perda was peering out the door.

69
00:03:20.827 --> 00:03:22.789
"There's the contraption!"

70
00:03:23.729 --> 00:03:26.090
Zann couldn't believe he hadn't noticed it right away.

71
00:03:26.851 --> 00:03:30.856
It was near the gnarled old tree, just to one side of the wormhole.

72
00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:33.597
"It looks so evil!"

73
00:03:34.317 --> 00:03:35.538
Gliss whispered with a shiver.

74
00:03:36.278 --> 00:03:37.018
Darb nodded.

75
00:03:37.038 --> 00:03:40.819
"It doesn't look much different than it did when we saw it in the Far Frontier."

76
00:03:40.839 --> 00:03:44.060
"Yes." Wyssa sounded relieved.

77
00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.241
"It's still not finished.

78
00:03:46.821 --> 00:03:49.722
Otherwise we would be too late to stop Morb."

79
00:03:49.742 --> 00:03:52.342
"How do you know it's not finished?"

80
00:03:52.802 --> 00:03:53.383
Perda asked.

81
00:03:53.403 --> 00:03:56.623
"That's what I started to tell you."

82
00:03:57.264 --> 00:03:59.388
Wyssa glanced at Zann.

83
00:03:59.408 --> 00:04:05.210
"I'm pretty certain that Morb plans to place the Mask of Zanta in the empty space on top.

84
00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:08.111
That's the most powerful relic there is.

85
00:04:08.771 --> 00:04:16.133
If we don't stop him, the results will be—" "Don't give away the surprise, Wyssa," a voice interrupted.

86
00:04:16.973 --> 00:04:17.953
Zann spun around.

87
00:04:17.973 --> 00:04:20.234
"Morb!" he exclaimed.

88
00:04:21.014 --> 00:04:24.155
The villain had just stepped out of the shadows at the back of the hut.

89
00:04:24.995 --> 00:04:26.816
Zann turned again, planning to run.

90
00:04:27.672 --> 00:04:30.514
But several trolls now blocked the hut's one opening.

91
00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:34.378
"Don't even think about trying to zap away," Morb warned.

92
00:04:34.398 --> 00:04:38.361
"The spell I've placed over Wormwood won't allow that."

93
00:04:39.201 --> 00:04:42.304
He pointed a finger toward Zing, who was already whistling again.

94
00:04:43.225 --> 00:04:45.066
The little dragon dropped like a rock.

95
00:04:45.967 --> 00:04:47.268
"Hey!" Darb cried.

96
00:04:47.288 --> 00:04:49.670
"Immobilization spells are illegal!"

97
00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:52.012
"Haven't you caught on yet?"

98
00:04:52.712 --> 00:04:54.034
Morb sounded amused.

99
00:04:54.054 --> 00:04:56.796
"The old rules don't apply anymore.

100
00:04:57.416 --> 00:05:01.358
I'm in charge now, and that means that I make the rules!"

101
00:05:02.619 --> 00:05:05.701
He reached into his robe and pulled out the Mask of Zanta.

102
00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:07.442
Wyssa gasped.

103
00:05:08.222 --> 00:05:09.162
"You can't!"

104
00:05:09.182 --> 00:05:11.324
"Silence, old woman."

105
00:05:11.964 --> 00:05:13.965
Morb held up the Mask, studying it.

106
00:05:13.985 --> 00:05:16.106
"It's beautiful, isn't it?

107
00:05:16.726 --> 00:05:18.707
Terrifying, but beautiful."

108
00:05:18.727 --> 00:05:21.709
"It's beautiful," Wyssa snapped.

109
00:05:21.729 --> 00:05:24.571
"But it's wasted on that thing out there."

110
00:05:25.791 --> 00:05:26.932
"My contraption?"

111
00:05:27.536 --> 00:05:28.777
Morb raised an eyebrow.

112
00:05:28.797 --> 00:05:30.358
"What do you mean?"

113
00:05:30.378 --> 00:05:35.342
"I thought you would try to take over Magica again," Wyssa said.

114
00:05:35.362 --> 00:05:40.345
"But there's no way you can do that with a travel contraption."

115
00:05:40.365 --> 00:05:42.627
"A travel contraption?"

116
00:05:42.947 --> 00:05:43.627
Perda echoed.

117
00:05:43.647 --> 00:05:45.308
"Is that what it is?"

118
00:05:46.449 --> 00:05:47.170
Morb chuckled.

119
00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:50.972
"Yes, the crazy old woman is correct," he said.

120
00:05:50.992 --> 00:05:52.433
"But don't fret.

121
00:05:52.934 --> 00:05:56.136
I doubt anyone will be disappointed by what I have planned.

122
00:05:56.832 --> 00:05:59.513
Horrified, yes, but not disappointed.

123
00:06:00.033 --> 00:06:04.674
The only thing that contraption has to do is get me safely through the wormhole."

124
00:06:05.514 --> 00:06:07.975
He pointed one bony finger toward the tree.

125
00:06:07.995 --> 00:06:13.597
"And then pull the Wormwood tree in after me."

126
00:06:13.617 --> 00:06:14.957
"No!" Wyssa blurted out.

127
00:06:15.777 --> 00:06:17.638
Zann was confused by Wyssa's panic.

128
00:06:18.078 --> 00:06:21.459
Did it really matter if Morb took the Wormwood tree through the wormhole?

129
00:06:22.259 --> 00:06:22.979
Morb laughed.

130
00:06:23.599 --> 00:06:26.120
"So you finally figured it out, hmm?"

131
00:06:26.496 --> 00:06:27.156
He taunted her.

132
00:06:27.176 --> 00:06:30.698
"It sure took you a long time, Wyssa."

133
00:06:31.458 --> 00:06:32.238
"What is it?"

134
00:06:32.719 --> 00:06:33.339
Gliss asked.

135
00:06:33.859 --> 00:06:35.300
"What did you figure out?"

136
00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:37.160
Wyssa looked grim.

137
00:06:38.001 --> 00:06:38.941
"That tree.

138
00:06:39.862 --> 00:06:41.302
It's the Source."

139
00:06:41.322 --> 00:06:43.563
"Huh?" Zann said.

140
00:06:43.583 --> 00:06:47.585
"The source You mean the Source of all magic?"

141
00:06:47.605 --> 00:06:49.806
"The Source is real?"

142
00:06:50.206 --> 00:06:50.726
Perda said.

143
00:06:50.746 --> 00:06:53.067
"Oh, yes, it's real."

144
00:06:53.667 --> 00:06:55.188
Morb sounded pleased with himself.

145
00:06:55.772 --> 00:06:59.898
"That tree pulls all of Magica's energy from the vortex."

146
00:06:59.918 --> 00:07:03.623
"But that means Zann began slowly.

147
00:07:03.643 --> 00:07:11.214
"It means," Wyssa said, "that removing it would leave Magica with no magic energy at all!"
